examples.json: the Markdown input of every example of two specifications, as marked's own test suite
holds them at marked v18.1.3 (https://github.com/markedjs/marked, commit
ba50aa95636ac8f97f46446bbfeb04592ed22216):

  cm-001 to cm-652   test/specs/commonmark/commonmark.0.31.2.json (git blob
                     e695ef9f606c8ae99284003c800c597ba8eab94e): every example of the CommonMark Spec,
                     version 0.31.2 (2024-01-28), https://spec.commonmark.org/0.31.2/
  gfm-<n>            test/specs/gfm/gfm.0.29.json (git blob 6b6ce22d6a2e1d367929d0af8805af301ac7b56f): the
                     28 examples of the GitHub Flavored Markdown Spec, version 0.29-gfm (2019-04-06), that
                     its extensions add (tables, task list items, strikethrough, autolinks, disallowed raw
                     HTML), https://github.github.com/gfm/

Each row keeps the example's number, its section (a GFM section with " (extension)" for marked's
"[extension] " prefix) and its markdown exactly; the specs' expected HTML is left out, since the
competition's expected HTML is what marked renders, never the spec's.

